			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Enforce PascalCase paths in FrontendCommand module\n\nUpdate the `Track::FrontendCommand` module to align with the project-wide PascalCase naming convention and strict path resolution required by Tauri's command macros.\n\nIn `DispatchFrontendCommand.rs`, correct the `CreateEffectForRequest` import to use the full PascalCase path with explicit function aliasing (`CreateEffectForRequest::Fn as CreateEffectForRequest`), replacing the previous shorthand segment. In `mod.rs`, remove legacy `pub use` re-exports and the `pub mod` exposure pattern that allowed flat imports. Replace them with an explicit `#![allow(non_snake_case)]` directive and documentation comments.\n\nThis enforces that callers must spell out the full double-segment paths (e.g., `Track::FrontendCommand::DispatchFrontendCommand::DispatchFrontendCommand`). This structure is mandatory for `tauri::generate_handler!` to correctly locate the `__cmd__` companion symbols while maintaining PascalCase file and module names, ensuring consistency across the Mountain crate and resolving potential symbol resolution issues in the IPC layer.",
