			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Enforce PascalCase paths in Track module imports\n\nUpdate the `Track` module tree to align with the project-wide PascalCase naming convention and strict path resolution required by Tauri's command macros.\n\nIn `Source/Track/Webview/MountainWebviewPostMessageFromGuest.rs`, correct the `ApplicationState` import to use the full PascalCase path `ApplicationState::State::ApplicationState::ApplicationState`, replacing the previous snake_case segment.\n\nIn `Source/Track/Webview/mod.rs` and `Source/Track/mod.rs`, remove legacy `pub use` re-exports and snake_case module declarations. Replace them with explicit `#![allow(non_snake_case)]` directives and comments documenting that callers must spell out the full double-segment paths (e.g., `Track::UIRequest::ResolveUIRequest::ResolveUIRequest`). This structure is mandatory for `tauri::generate_handler!` to correctly locate the `__cmd__` companion symbols while maintaining PascalCase file and module names.\n\nThis ensures consistency across the Mountain crate and resolves potential symbol resolution issues in the IPC layer.",
